\emph default
 and the true 
\emph on
distribution mean
\emph default
 against the values of 
\begin_inset Formula $N$
\end_inset

 given.
 What sort of trend do they give? Is that trend consistent? When, typically,
 are the sample based estimates of the mean worst?
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
What is the true 
\emph on
second moment
\emph default
 of the distribution you've sampled form?
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
For each point, plot the squared difference between the 
\emph on
sample based estimate
\emph default
 of the second moment and the 
\emph on
true
\emph default
 second moment of the distribution.
 Is the trend similar to that of the sample based mean? Are the estimates
 of the second moment typically better or worse? Why do you think this is
 the case?
\end_layout

